senses.gloss:
kṣudra (= kṣaudra, q.v.; cf. Pali Lex. khudda, honey, Abhidh., see Childers),
(1) ep. of madhu, = kṣaudra(ṃ) madhu, (a kind of) honey: kṣudramadhusadṛśāni phalāni Mv 〔ii.107.4〕; 〔108.4, 13〕; kṣudra-madhu (˚dhv, ˚dhum) aneḍakaṃ (once ˚ko; or anel˚) Mv 〔i.339.8〕; 〔340.13〕; 〔341.7〕 (vv.ll. kṣaudra-, kṣudro, kṣudraṃ; at least 1 ms. each time kṣudra-);
(2) adj., honey-like, honeyed, honey-, sweet: with yvāgu, gruel, Mv 〔ii.84.9—10〕 (prose) kṣudrāye ca yvāgūye ghaṭikā haste; 〔13, 16〕 yvāgu (˚gū) kṣudrā (n. sg.); kṣudra-kṣudrāṇi phalāni Mv 〔iii.145.2〕, see s.v. kṣudra-pāka, in which kṣudra-seems to = Skt. svādu-.
